## iti82
iti82:1.1 | S: This was said by the Buddha, the Perfected One: that is what I heard. | T: This was said by the Blessed One, said by the Arahant, so I have heard:
iti82:2.1 | S: “Mendicants, these three cries are uttered among the gods on occasion. | T: “Monks, these three divine sounds sound forth among the devas on appropriate occasions.
iti82:2.2 | S: What three? | T: Which three?
iti82:2.3 | S: When a noble disciple shaves off their hair and beard, dresses in ocher robes, and goes forth from the lay life to homelessness, the gods cry out: | T: When a disciple of the noble ones, shaving off his hair & beard, clothing himself in the ochre robe, makes up his mind to go forth from the home life into homelessness, on that occasion the divine sound sounds forth among the devas:
iti82:2.4 | S: ‘This noble disciple intends to join battle with Māra!’ | T: ‘This disciple of the noble ones has made up his mind to do battle with Māra.’
iti82:2.5 | S: This is the first occasion a cry is uttered among the gods. | T: This is the first divine sound that sounds forth among the devas on appropriate occasions.
iti82:3.1 | S: Furthermore, when a noble disciple meditates pursuing the development of the seven qualities on the side of awakening, the gods cry out: | T: “When a disciple of the noble ones lives devoted to developing the seven [sets of] qualities that are wings to awakening, on that occasion the divine sound sounds forth among the devas:
iti82:3.2 | S: ‘This noble disciple is joining battle with Māra!’ | T: ‘This disciple of the noble ones is doing battle with Māra.’
iti82:3.3 | S: This is the second occasion a cry is uttered among the gods. | T: This is the second divine sound that sounds forth among the devas on appropriate occasions.
iti82:4.1 | S: Furthermore, when a noble disciple realizes the undefiled freedom of heart and freedom by wisdom. And they live having realized it with their own insight in this very life due to the ending of defilements, the gods cry out: | T: “When a disciple of the noble ones, through the ending of effluents, enters & remains in the effluent-free awareness-release & discernment-release, directly knowing & realizing it for himself right in the here-&-now, on that occasion the divine sound sounds forth among the devas:
iti82:4.2 | S: ‘This noble disciple has won victory in battle, establishing himself as foremost in battle!’ | T: ‘This disciple of the noble ones, having won the battle, now rules victorious at the head of the battle.’
iti82:4.3 | S: This is the third occasion a cry is uttered among the gods. | T: This is the third divine sound that sounds forth among the devas on appropriate occasions.
iti82:4.4 | S: These are the three cries that are uttered among the gods on occasion.” | T: “These are the three divine sounds that sound forth among the devas on appropriate occasions.”
iti82:4.5 | S: The Buddha spoke this matter. | T: (none)
iti82:4.6 | S: On this it is said: | T: (none)
iti82:5.1 | S: “Seeing the winner of the battle— | T: Seeing he’s won the battle
iti82:5.2 | S: a disciple of the Buddha, | T: –the disciple of the Rightly Self-awakened One–
iti82:5.3 | S: great of heart, intrepid— | T: even the devas pay homage to this great one, thoroughly mature.
iti82:5.4 | S: even the deities revere them: | T: (none)
iti82:6.1 | S: ‘Homage to you, O thoroughbred! | T: “Homage to you, O thoroughbred man–
iti82:6.2 | S: You won a battle hard to win! | T: you who have won the hard victory,
iti82:6.3 | S: Having defeated the army of death, | T: defeating the army of Death,
iti82:6.4 | S: your liberation is unhindered.’ | T: unhindered in emancipation.”
iti82:7.1 | S: And so the deities revere the one, | T: Thus they pay homage, the devas,
iti82:7.2 | S: who has achieved their heart’s desire. | T: to one who has reached the heart’s goal,
iti82:7.3 | S: For they see nothing in them by means of which | T: for they see in him no means
iti82:7.4 | S: they might fall under the sway of Death.” | T: that would bring him under Death’s sway.
